# Example of .env.dev, the development stack's optional overrides. Without a .env.dev at the repository root,
# copy it there (ignored by git), uncomment what you need and restrict it: chmod 600 .env.dev. When .env.dev
# exists, never copy over it: add only the lines you need. Example only: never commit values.
#
# Not here: the database password and the keys. scripts/local.sh generates them into <data dir>/stack.env
# (default ~/.local/share/adiutor-dev/stack.env). Keys an older .env.dev already sets keep winning over that file;
# keep them as they are, or move them there by hand as whole values (the data they encrypted needs them).

# A reverse proxy in front of the stack (docs/deployment.md, section 7). The port is published on every interface.
# ADIUTOR_PORT=
# The URL the browser opens through the proxy; browser changes from another Origin are refused.
# ADIUTOR_PUBLIC_URL=
# The proxy's address, only when the proxy replaces the X-Forwarded-For header that clients send.
# ADIUTOR_TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# Optional: these lock their field in Settings. Leave them unset to manage them in Settings.
# ADIUTOR_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# ADIUTOR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# ADIUTOR_PRIVATE_DOMAINS=
